// Local-only wrangler config for @hb/db: applies migrations to (and seeds) the shared local D1.
// Never deployed. Production database_id is set by the client at deploy time (non-goal here).
//
// SHARED LOCAL D1 CONVENTION (every Worker config in this repo must match it):
//   binding        "DB"
//   database_name  "hb-destockage"
//   database_id    "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000d1b"   (local placeholder; local state is keyed by it)
//   migrations_dir "<repo>/packages/db/migrations"
//   persist path   "<worktree>/.wrangler/hb-local"  → from apps/<x>/: --persist-to ../../.wrangler/hb-local
//                                                  → from packages/db/: --persist-to ../../.wrangler/hb-local
//   R2             binding "MEDIA", bucket_name "hb-media"  (same persist path)
// So web, admin, jobs, the seed and the e2e harness all see ONE seeded database and ONE bucket per
// worktree. Verified: two configs with this database_id and persist path read the same SQLite file
// (artifacts/DB-1/d1-smoke.log, artifacts/DB-3/seed-run.log).
//
// Fill it (idempotent; safe to re-run; never touches orders, customers, events, audit):
//   npm run seed -w @hb/db                    # migrations + data/ + dev admin users + photos → R2
//   npm run migrate:local -w @hb/db           # migrations only
// The seed refuses --remote, a non-local database_id, ENV other than development, and
// NODE_ENV=production: it writes placeholder fees and dev users (packages/db/src/seed/guard.ts).
// Reset: delete <worktree>/.wrangler/hb-local and seed again.
{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "hb-db-local",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-11-01",
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "hb-destockage",
      "database_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000d1b",
      "migrations_dir": "migrations"
    }
  ],
  // Local R2 for photos (same bucket and binding as apps/admin and apps/jobs).
  "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "MEDIA", "bucket_name": "hb-media" }]
}
